alderpointdns (0.4.0~beta4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * 0.4.0~beta3-1 was built and tag-created but withdrawn before any
    GitHub Release was published (a first prerelease publish had to be
    deleted and its tag name became permanently unusable under GitHub's
    immutable-releases policy); no beta3 package was ever distributed. All
    of its changes are carried forward unchanged in this release.
  * Fixed filtering deployments incorrectly failing when a downloaded allow
    rule returned a valid DNS response without an IPv4 A record. Cache-only
    changes now report and roll back component state accurately.
  * Fixed a production incident in which the analytics writer thread could
    die silently while its parent process kept reporting healthy: closed a
    SQLite connection-descriptor leak present across most of the web app's
    database call sites, added retry-with-backoff and an independent
    heartbeat to the analytics writer, and corrected System Status severity
    reporting (Warning/Error/Info) for these conditions.
  * Fixed a blocklist zero-rule ambiguity: a source that legitimately
    compiles to zero rules is now distinguished from a fetch/parse
    failure, IPv6-only hosts-format sinkhole entries now compile
    correctly, AdGuard `$dnsrewrite` handling was corrected, and
    System Status now reports real, distinct blocklist health states
    instead of collapsing them together.
  * Fixed the local test-deb builder silently omitting the admin CLI
    entry point and the `alderpointdns-notify.timer` unit from built
    packages.
  * Scrubbed a real home-LAN domain and IP addresses that had been
    reintroduced into test fixtures.
  * Documentation refresh covering the recent Administration,
    Notifications, migration, and reliability work.
  * Added the accompanying automated test coverage for the fixes above,
    including deterministic connection-lifecycle tests, a web-traffic
    file-descriptor regression test, and a concurrency test exercising
    live web requests against the database alongside the analytics
    writer under lock contention.

 -- Alderpoint DNS Maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 15:45:00 -0600

alderpointdns (0.4.0~beta2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Established the alderpointdns system account, paths, and environment
    variables used by the package: package, service, path, and
    environment-variable names all use alderpointdns/ALDERPOINTDNS_
    consistently, including the system user/group that the daemons run
    as and own their data, log, and config directories under.
  * Fixed a live-database backup race: scripts/backup.sh now takes a
    SQLite online-backup-API snapshot instead of tarring the live WAL-mode
    database file directly.
  * Added a collapsible desktop sidebar with an icon-only rail, flyout
    submenus, keyboard/focus support, and a localStorage-persisted,
    flash-free collapsed state; the mobile drawer is unaffected.
  * Reworked Local DNS records into compact, single-line, truncated rows
    with a collapsed-by-default row editor, fixing hostnames/comments that
    previously wrapped mid-word.
  * Reworked DNS Settings upstream resolver actions into a Save/Enable
    primary row plus a reorder/delete overflow menu.
  * Replaced Blocklists' free-text category field with managed categories
    (create/rename/merge/delete-with-reassignment) and a compact,
    filterable/sortable source table.
  * Replaced System Status Recent Logs' raw, permission-denied journalctl
    output with a narrowly-scoped, sudoers-allowlisted log helper
    (alderpointdns, alderpointdns-analytics, named, dnsdist only) that
    returns sanitized, structured log entries with service/severity/line
    filters.
  * Fixed Dashboard System Health cards splitting words like "Healthy" and
    "DNSSEC" mid-character on narrow layouts.
  * build-deb.sh now derives the Debian package version from VERSION
    (0.4.0-beta.2 -> 0.4.0~beta2-1) instead of embedding the semver-style
    string verbatim.
  * Fixed a first-clean-install failure where all four core services
    crash-looped after a "successful" install: secrets.env/dnsdist API
    and web credentials are group-readable (0640, not 0600); the
    database is chowned to alderpointdns after generation, without
    broadening ownership of the root-owned, world-readable compiled
    BIND/dnsdist config; named's AppArmor local override is installed
    and reloaded; postinst now generates unique per-install dnsdist
    console/web/API credentials, hashes the web password/API key with
    dnsdist's own hashPassword() before writing dnsdist.conf (no more
    plaintext-credential warning, no weaker auth), and preserves those
    credentials across upgrades while regenerating them on a genuine
    purge + reinstall. dnsdist.conf's newRemoteLogger/RemoteLogResponseAction
    calls and DoH3/DoQ/DNSCrypt listener setup are now compatible with
    (and gracefully degrade against) Debian 13's own archive dnsdist
    package, and the package now requires dnsdist (>= 2.0.0) so
    installing without the documented PowerDNS repository fails cleanly
    at dependency resolution instead of silently pulling an incompatible
    build. postinst validates configuration and verifies all four
    services reach the active state before reporting success;
    StartLimitBurst/StartLimitIntervalSec caps prevent runaway restart
    loops. Added tests/test_clean_install_container.sh (fresh Debian 13 +
    systemd container, no inherited dev-machine state) and
    tests/test_deb_package_contents.sh (static built-package inspection).
  * Finalized the project license: source-available under the PolyForm
    Noncommercial License 1.0.0 (LICENSE), not open source; commercial
    use requires a separate license (COMMERCIAL_LICENSING.md). Added
    COPYRIGHT, CONTRIBUTOR_LICENSE_AGREEMENT.md, TRADEMARKS.md, and
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. The package now installs LICENSE/copyright/
    COMMERCIAL_LICENSING.md/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md under
    /usr/share/doc/alderpointdns/.
  * Fixed a second clean-install failure introduced by the previous fix:
    requiring dnsdist (>= 2.0.0) meant the package could not be installed
    at all on a genuinely fresh Debian 13 system, since that version is
    only available from the PowerDNS project's own (non-default) apt
    repository and a .deb cannot configure a third-party repository to
    satisfy its own dependency before apt resolves it. Depends now reads
    dnsdist (>= 1.9.0), the lowest bound Debian 13's own archive dnsdist
    (1.9.x) satisfies, so `apt-get install -y ./alderpointdns_*.deb`
    resolves and installs cleanly with no third-party repository, key, or
    pin required. Debian's own dnsdist build supports plain DNS, DoH, DoT,
    DNSCrypt, and everything the BIND backend integration needs (packet
    cache, ACLs, analytics logging, authenticated web/API access), but
    lacks DNS-over-QUIC/DNS-over-HTTP/3; DoQ/DoH3 now ship disabled by
    default (packaging/dnsdist.service.d/alderpointdns.conf) and
    app/encryption.py detects the installed dnsdist's actual capabilities
    (parsing `dnsdist --version`'s feature list) both to keep unsupported
    protocols out of a deployment -- degrading just that protocol with a
    clear message instead of failing/rolling back the whole deployment --
    and to render them as unsupported, not enabled or broken, on the
    Encryption Settings page. The PowerDNS repository remains available
    (docs/dnsdist.md) as an optional upgrade path for DoQ/DoH3, detected
    automatically with no package reinstall required. Rewrote
    tests/test_clean_install_container.sh to install strictly from stock
    Debian 13 repositories (`apt-get install -y ./package.deb`, no
    repo.powerdns.com reference permitted anywhere in the run) and to
    verify service state, DNS resolution, credential handling, and
    reboot-equivalent restart behavior against that stock build.
  * Fixed the Encryption Settings page (and the dashboard's System
    Health cert card) throwing a 500 on a genuinely fresh install:
    /etc/alderpointdns/certs was root:_dnsdist mode 0750, so the
    unprivileged alderpointdns web process -- in neither group -- got
    PermissionError on a bare stat() of its own certificate, despite the
    certificate file itself being world-readable (0644). Changed the
    directory to mode 0751 (traversable, but still no read/write for
    "other", so the 0640 private key stays unreadable); ensure_tls_cert.sh
    now applies this unconditionally, including on upgrades where
    certificate material already exists. Also made unsupported-protocol
    enforcement symmetric: encryption.enforce_capabilities(), factored
    out of deploy_encryption(), is now applied when saving Encryption
    Settings too, so a forged POST cannot persist doq_enabled=1/
    doh3_enabled=1 on an installation whose dnsdist lacks that capability.
  * Web interface usability pass from beta feedback: a reusable
    pending-action button state (disables, swaps to an in-progress label
    with a spinner, sets aria-busy, restores on failure) applied to every
    form site-wide instead of per-page handlers; restructured status-tile
    cards (name centered on top, status badge centered below it, not
    beside the name) across System Health, System Status, Encryption,
    Replication, Backup, and DNS Settings; a shared centered Actions-column
    table utility applied to Local DNS, Blocklists, Custom Rules, DNS
    Settings upstreams, Backup, and Replication; a recognizable icon,
    accessible name, and tooltip for the collapsed-sidebar Logout control;
    and sidebar nav sections that collapse again after opening (including
    a section containing the active page) with expand/collapse state now
    persisted across navigation.
  * Added a first-class Pi-hole Migration panel to Import and Migration,
    alongside AdGuard Home's, explaining the supported Pi-hole export
    format and warning that group assignments have no Alderpoint DNS
    equivalent. The Pi-hole importer backend and preview/apply/rollback
    pipeline already existed; only the dedicated UI panel and end-to-end
    route tests against the synthetic Pi-hole fixture were added.
  * Closed import-idempotency gaps: blocklist sources are now also matched
    by URL (not just name) so the same feed re-added under a different
    name is skipped instead of duplicated, and comment/invalid/unsupported
    custom-rule entries are now deduplicated the same way active rules
    already were. Local DNS records, client aliases, and upstream
    resolvers were already correctly deduplicated. Added tests proving
    repeated AdGuard/Pi-hole imports (as separate jobs) do not increase
    any destination table's row count.

